WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.918
Turbulence is physics'

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:03.451
hardest unsolved problem

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:05.228
Turbulence is called

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.218
the hardest remaining

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:07.232
problem in classical

00:00:07.044 --> 00:00:07.669
physics

00:00:07.728 --> 00:00:08.494
and we still

00:00:08.306 --> 00:00:09.308
do not exactly

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:09.732
know how it

00:00:09.544 --> 00:00:10.181
works

00:00:10.702 --> 00:00:11.916
More than 200

00:00:11.728 --> 00:00:13.072
people were seriously

00:00:12.884 --> 00:00:14.074
injured in turbulence

00:00:13.886 --> 00:00:15.041
on US airplanes

00:00:14.853 --> 00:00:17.494
between 2009 and 2023

00:00:17.695 --> 00:00:18.838
according to FAA

00:00:18.662 --> 00:00:19.251
data

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:20.969
Now terabytes of

00:00:20.781 --> 00:00:21.889
crowdsourced flight

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:22.655
data and new

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:23.410
machine learning

00:00:23.446 --> 00:00:24.483
may help pilots

00:00:24.306 --> 00:00:25.155
get ten to

00:00:24.967 --> 00:00:26.051
fifteen minutes of

00:00:25.863 --> 00:00:27.089
warning before the

00:00:26.901 --> 00:00:28.127
choppiness hits

00:00:28.662 --> 00:00:29.676
Full story on

00:00:29.487 --> 00:00:30.383
the dashboard
